prompt:
Create one original 1536×1024 true-transparent RGBA spritesheet for Moxie Capwell of Moonmorel Hex performing an eight-pose right-facing basketball steal. Use both supplied canon references. Moxie is the same adult human woman with pale skin, lavender eyes, very long thick lavender hair in a high ponytail with small gold tie, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and purple high-top shoes; mature athletic human build. Preserve face, eye color, ponytail silhouette/tie, kit and anatomy consistently. No male, witch hat, beard, monster, robot or different athlete.

Draw crisp readable 1990s arcade basketball sprite art with consistent camera/scale. Exactly eight distinct complete full-body poses in a strict 4-column by 2-row grid, row-major, with generous true-transparent gutters and outer margins. Keep all hair, limbs and shoes in each cell. Do not draw any ball: the game renders it separately. No sphere, seams, hoop, rim, floor, court, shadow, effects, glow, labels, text, borders, teammate or scene. Hands are empty.

Sequence:
0 defensive stance, facing right, knees bent and eyes on opponent;
1 shuffle close, drop center of gravity, near hand reaches cautiously;
2 sharp step-in and turn shoulders, one open hand sweeps toward the imagined ball;
3 STEAL contact at simulation tick5: empty palm snaps toward the ball path at waist height, fingers spread;
4 retract the empty hand and rotate hips away from the opponent;
5 pivot into a protected stance, arms counterbalance;
6 begin moving right with the ball now separate and off-screen/near court;
7 settle into a controlled defensive recovery, hands visible and empty.

Make actions distinct and connected; show a believable reach without clipping the ponytail or hiding Moxie’s face. Keep the same adult human features and purple/silver kit. Return only true-transparent RGBA with alpha-zero background, no matte, checkerboard, halo, haze or speckles.
